      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Noturus leptacanthus Jordan, 1877</li><li>Common names: Speckled Madtom; Småplettet Giftmalle (Denmark)</li><li>Synonym: Schilbeodes leptacanthus</li><li>Etymology: From the Greek notos, meaning back, and oura, meaning tail, in reference to the confluent adipose and caudal fins.</li><li>IUCN Red List category: Least Concern (last assessed 2012)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1301",
      "html": "<p>North America: North American Atlantic drainages, Florida waters and Gulf Coast drainages.</p><p>Type locality: Silver Creek, 1 mile above its junction with Etowah River, near Rome, Floyd County, Georgia, U.S.A.</p>"
    },
